 ("What is the Fitzpatrick skin type classification?", ["I always burns never tans; II usually burns tans minimally; III sometimes burns tans gradually; IV burns minimally tans well (most North Indians); V rarely burns tans profusely (South Indians); VI never burns deeply pigmented — guides phototherapy dosing and laser settings"]),
 ("What is the UV index and photoprotection advice?", ["UV index ≥3 — protection needed; avoid 10 am–4 pm sun, seek shade, protective clothing (UPF ≥30), wide-brimmed hat, broad-spectrum SPF ≥30 sunscreen 2 mg/cm² reapplied every 2 h, sunglasses"]),
 ("Classify sunscreens (PYQ: classify sunscreens).", ["Organic (chemical) UV absorbers: UVB — PABA derivatives, cinnamates (octinoxate), salicylates, octocrylene; UVA — benzophenones (oxybenzone), avobenzone, ecamsule, newer broad-spectrum (bemotrizinol/ Tinosorb S, bisoctrizole/ Tinosorb M)", "Inorganic (physical) blockers: zinc oxide, titanium dioxide (micronised/ nano); iron oxides for visible light", "Ideal sunscreen: broad spectrum UVA+UVB, photostable, water-resistant, cosmetically acceptable, non-irritant, non-comedogenic"]),
